"Two springboards of heights of 1 and 3 metres."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This competition consisted of two compulsory dives from 1 metre and two compulsory dives from 3 metres, followed by three optionals from 3 metres, which could be selected from a table of 18 allowable dives.  Germany swept the first four places.  After the compulsory dives, " [:a {:href "/athletes/47959"} "Albert Zürner"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/47816"} "Paul Günther"] " led, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/50407"} "Johan Jansson"] " close behind them.  Günther dove brilliantly during the optional dives and was placed first by four of the five judges.  The competition for the bronze medal was very close, with total ordinal scores of 22-23-24 given to Jansson, Zürner, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/47872"} "Hans Luber"] ".  The fourth-place finisher, Albert Zürner, was the defending Olympic champion from this event in " [:a {:href "/results/54013"} "London 1908"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47816"} "Paul Günther"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "9 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47872"} "Hans Luber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "6 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "9 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47778"} "Kurt Behrens"]] [:td {} [: